    <section id="ch5">
      <h2>5. Association Testing & Linear Mixed Models (LMM)</h2>

      <h3>Marginal Testing & Wald Test Statistic</h3>
      <p>
        For quantitative traits, single-marker regression tests <Katex tex="H_0: \beta_j = 0" />:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">OLS Marginal Regression & Wald Z-Score</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\hat{\beta}_j = \frac{\mathbf{x}_j^T \mathbf{y}}{\mathbf{x}_j^T \mathbf{x}_j}, \quad \text{SE}(\hat{\beta}_j) = \sqrt{\frac{\hat{\sigma}^2}{\mathbf{x}_j^T \mathbf{x}_j}}, \quad z_j = \frac{\hat{\beta}_j}{\text{SE}(\hat{\beta}_j)}, \quad P = 2 \Phi(-|z_j|)" display={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Logistic Regression & The Liability Threshold Model</h3>
      <p>
        For binary case-control traits, logistic regression models disease probability <Katex tex="\pi_i = P(y_i = 1 \mid \mathbf{x}_i)" />:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Logistic Regression Link & Liability Threshold Heritability Conversion</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\log\left(\frac{\pi_i}{1 - \pi_i}\right) = \mathbf{w}_i^T \boldsymbol{\alpha} + \beta_j X_{ij}, \qquad h^2_{\text{liability}} = h^2_{\text{observed}} \frac{K(1 - K)}{z_K^2} \frac{K(1 - K)}{P(1 - P)}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <strong>Lee et al. (2011) Conversion:</strong> <Katex tex="K" /> = Population disease prevalence &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="P" /> = Sample proportion of cases &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="z_K" /> = Standard normal density height at threshold <Katex tex="\Phi^{-1}(1 - K)" />.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Confounding Structures & Genomic Inflation (λ_GC)</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Genomic Inflation Factor</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\lambda_{\text{GC}} = \frac{\text{median}(\chi^2_1, \chi^2_2, \dots, \chi^2_M)}{0.454936}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="0.454936" /> is the median of a central <Katex tex="\chi^2_1" /> distribution. In large cohorts (<Katex tex="N > 100,000" />), polygenicity naturally inflates <Katex tex="\lambda_{\text{GC}} > 1.2" />, making LDSC intercept the gold standard for separating confounding from true biology.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Computational Evolution of Linear Mixed Models</h3>
      <div class="paper-table-wrap">
        <table class="paper-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Method / Tool</th>
              <th>Algorithmic Breakthrough</th>
              <th>Computational Complexity</th>
              <th>Cohort Scalability</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>GEMMA / FaST-LMM (2012)</strong></td>
              <td>Spectral eigen-decomposition of GRM <Katex tex="\mathbf{A} = \mathbf{U}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{U}^T" />.</td>
