    <section id="ch6">
      <h2>6. Bayesian Fine-Mapping & Causal Variant Prioritization</h2>

      <h3>The Fundamental LD Confounding Equation</h3>
      <p>
        Because of Linkage Disequilibrium, the marginal GWAS effect estimates <Katex tex="\hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}" /> are linear combinations of all true causal effects <Katex tex="\boldsymbol{\beta}_{\text{true}}" /> weighted by the LD correlation matrix <Katex tex="\mathbf{R}" />:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">LD Confounding Matrix Equation</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbb{E}[\hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}] = \mathbf{R} \boldsymbol{\beta}_{\text{true}}" display={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Wakefield's Approximate Bayes Factor (ABF, 2009)</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Wakefield ABF Formulation</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\text{ABF}_j = \sqrt{\frac{V_j}{V_j + W}} \exp\left( \frac{z_j^2}{2} \frac{W}{V_j + W} \right)" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="V_j = \text{SE}(\hat{\beta}_j)^2" /> = Measurement error variance &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="W = \sigma_0^2" /> = Prior variance of true effect sizes.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Sum of Single Effects (SuSiE, Wang & Stephens 2020)</h3>
      <p>
        SuSiE decomposes a polygenic locus with up to <Katex tex="L" /> distinct causal signals into a sum of single-effect vectors:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">SuSiE Generative Model</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbf{y} = \sum_{l=1}^{L} \mathbf{X} \boldsymbol{\gamma}_l b_l + \boldsymbol{\epsilon}, \quad \boldsymbol{\gamma}_l \sim \text{Multinomial}(1, \boldsymbol{\pi}), \quad b_l \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_l^2), \quad \boldsymbol{\epsilon} \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2 \mathbf{I})" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="\boldsymbol{\gamma}_l \in \{0, 1\}^M" /> = Indicator vector with exactly one non-zero entry designating the causal variant for signal <Katex tex="l" /> &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="\boldsymbol{\pi}" /> = Prior causal probabilities (uniform or informed by PolyFun/Sniff).
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        SuSiE fits this model via <strong>Iterative Bayesian Stepwise Selection (IBSS)</strong>, an exact coordinate ascent variational inference (CAVI) algorithm that outputs:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Posterior Inclusion Probability (PIP):</strong> <Katex tex="\text{PIP}_j = 1 - \prod_{l=1}^{L} (1 - \alpha_{lj})" />, representing the probability that variant <Katex tex="j" /> is causal.</li>
        <li><strong>95% Credible Sets (CS):</strong> The minimal set of variants that contains the causal variant with <Katex tex="\ge 95\%" /> posterior certainty.</li>
      </ul>

